site diagonal of the bounding box.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/1478ab18.py:35:    \"\"\"Paint the teal outline of the right triangle determined by the missing corner of the grey-marker square.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/1478ab18.py:40:    Find the one corner of the marker bounding square that has no marker. That missing corner is the right-angle vertex of a right isosceles triangle; paint its two axis-aligned legs and the opposite diagonal in teal, leaving existing marker pixels unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/1478ab18.py:42:    The present corner marker opposite the missing corner is a decoy; the three triangle vertices are the missing corner and the two marker corners adjacent to it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/1478ab18.py:97:    # step inward from the missing corner toward the opposite corner\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/a6f40cea.py:545:    # Place L-shaped components in random corners\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/f8f52ecc.py:117:    - Connect each consecutive pair by the shortest clear L-shaped path between the two components.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/faa9f03d.py:456:    \"\"\"Build L-shaped arm waypoints for _path_crossing_all / _path_through.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/cbebaa4b.py:265:    \"\"\"Draw an L-shaped path from *start* to *end*, preserving red (2) pixels.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/21897d95.py:255:    \"\"\"Find a 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker and return its corner position.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/21897d95.py:290:    - An optional 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker triggers 90-degree rotation of the output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/21897d95.py:297:    - A 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker controls rotation: ┐ (corner top-right) → CCW 90°, ┌ (corner top-left) → CW 90°.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:10:    - bg grid with monochrome 3-pixel L-shaped \"arrows\" (2x2 bbox missing one corner) and scattered colored wall pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:13:    - Each arrow fires a ray diagonally away from its missing corner, painting bg cells in its color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:41:        # direction away from missing corner\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/142ca369.py:170:            # Arrow = 3 corners of 2x2 bbox, missing corner opposite to fire direction\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/f560132c.py:318:LEGEND_THRESHOLD = {8: 4, 10: 5, 12: 9}       # min extent threshold per side for legend L-shape\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/f560132c.py:320:LEGEND_ARM_RANGE = range(1, 4)                 # arm width/height options for L-shape construction\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/f560132c.py:366:    \"\"\"Build an L-shaped legend piece mask anchored at (0,0) of the side*side grid.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/e3721c99.py:121:L_LAYOUT_MAX_SPAN = 24            # max legend line span for L-shaped layouts\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/e3721c99.py:280:    \"\"\"Place an L-shaped divider with legend panel in one corner.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/e509e548.py:24:    - Count L-shaped 2x2 bend patterns across all rotations.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/e509e548.py:46:        # Do this by building an L-shaped mask, and seeing how many times it appears in the sprite\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/34cfa167.py:105:    - Copy the anchor rectangle into the two missing corners of the implied\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/4522001f.py:23:    - The missing corner of the 2x2 fill square is the marker; its orientation\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/1e5d6875.py:20:    assert len(missing) == 1, \"2x2 L triomino must have exactly one missing corner\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/1e5d6875.py:43:    - The missing corner of each 2x2 L object identifies its diagonal axis, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/470c91de.py:57:    - Treat the teal pixel as the missing corner of its colored rectangle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/a2fd1cf0.py:11:    Draw a teal L-shaped path from the red pixel to the green pixel, moving horizontally first and then vertically.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/6e19193c.py:20:    - Each arrowhead is a small shape whose missing corner indicates its direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/9f236235.py:15:# Finally mirror along the x-axis.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/8618d23e.py:23:    The output is not a recoloring of either region; it inserts an L-shaped maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/a61ba2ce.py:19:    - Place it in the 4x4 output quadrant opposite its missing corner, preserving its orientation and color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/a61ba2ce.py:20:    - The missing corner of each sprite becomes one cell of the central 2x2 background hole.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/3aa6fb7a.py:20:    - Paint that missing corner blue while preserving all original pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/3aa6fb7a.py:44:        assert len(missing) == 1, \"each 2x2 box must have exactly one missing corner\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/3aa6fb7a.py:47:        assert g[r, c] == bg, \"missing corner must be background\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/3aa6fb7a.py:117:    \"\"\"Compute the oracle output by filling each detected L missing corner.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/3aa6fb7a.py:130:    \"\"\"Paint one L object in-place, leaving the sampled missing corner black.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/58c02a16.py:24:    The solid L-shaped secondary-color border is a legend, not output content; it supplies the color used when the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/54dc2872.py:52:    \"\"\"Move each marked L-shaped sprite onto the separate pixel matching its marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ac0c5833.py:93:    \"\"\"Copy the existing