 the marker's 2x2 box: top-left -> green, bottom-left -> yellow, bottom-right -> pink, top-right -> teal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ecaa0ec1.py:54:    - Three marker pixels form the outer corners of a missing-corner square whose missing corner touches one sprite corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ecaa0ec1.py:64:    - The marker pixels are rotation controls: the L-shaped group names the target corner, while the lone marker names the corner that must rotate into it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/1e97544e.py:103:# L-shape construction and sampling weights.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/18/code.py:106:    Marker corners are L-shapes:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/18/code.py:287:    - Away from the legend, active marker colors appear as diagonal pairs of L-shaped corners; optional non-legend\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d8e07eb2/D4/0/code.py:21:#     - Suppose a matched table cell contains a yellow L-shape in the inner 3x3.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/3/code.py:174:    Marker corners are L-shapes:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d8e07eb2/33/code.py:29:#      extra column that host a tiny L-shaped verdict badge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d8e07eb2/33/code.py:87:#    - The badge uses a fixed 5-pixel L-shape in the bottom-right corner, which\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d8e07eb2/33/code.py:210:    - Return only the cropped table area, plus a small bottom-right L-shaped\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d8e07eb2/D11/0/code.py:35:#       - place a 5-pixel L-shaped marker in the bottom-right corner\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/17/code.py:189:    Marker corners are L-shapes:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/31/code.py:26:#      size 2-4, such as dominoes, 3-lines, small L-shapes, or 2x2 blocks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/31/code.py:36:#   If a left-region dent is an L-shape at {(5,5),(6,5),(6,6)}, the original solver\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/31/code.py:40:#   one 3x3 patch for each member of the pair and turns the full L-shape teal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/20/code.py:76:    Marker corners are L-shapes:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d8e07eb2/11/code.py:26:#    - Example: if a cell contains a maroon L-shape on teal and it is queried,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d8e07eb2/11/code.py:28:#      the teal border and turns the maroon L-shape into a gray L-shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/de809cff/D9/0/code.py:20:#    while the new task keeps them intact and yields an irregular L-shaped patch.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/de809cff/D9/0/code.py:47:#    marks stay full 3x3 blocks while others become truncated wedges or L-shapes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/2/code.py:115:    Marker corners are L-shapes:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/9/code.py:148:    Marker corners are L-shapes:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/10/code.py:48:#    If the same region is L-shaped, the Manhattan depth-2 / depth-3 bands bend\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/10/code.py:315:        assert info is not None, \"each marker component must be a 3-cell L-shape\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/10/code.py:372:    - Outside the legend, every marker color appears as 2-3 separate pairs of 3-cell L-shapes, where each intended pair shares either one row or one column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/21/code.py:31:        because a directed cross is not an L-shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2d0172a1/D14/2/code.py:30:#       - old solver: row/col bands could produce a diagonal or L-shaped packing depending on bbox overlaps\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/4/code.py:432:    - Away from the legend, each marker color appears as one diagonal pair of L-shaped corner marks;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/25/code.py:117:    raise AssertionError(\"missing corner legend\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/5/code.py:25:        so TL is the missing corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/5/code.py:30:      - If the missing corner were TR or BL, the same TL-BR band would survive almost fully because\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/5/code.py:188:    \"\"\"Validate a 3-corner triangle group and return its bbox, corner map, and missing corner name.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/14/code.py:50:#    - Large black foreground objects remain simple bands / rectangles / L-shapes so that the new\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/13/code.py:130:    Marker corners are L-shapes:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d8e07eb2/10/code.py:22:#     - Suppose a matched table cell contains a yellow L-shape and an unmatched cell contains a blue T-shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/23/code.py:138:    Marker corners are L-shapes:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/35/code.py:75:#      insets, or L-shapes. Only a handful of interior anomalies are injected,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/22/code.py:121:    Marker corners are L-shapes:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/6/code.py:119:    Marker corners are L-shapes:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/39/code.py:55:- The original generator allowed visible L-shapes via occlusion. That breaks the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/12/code.py:122:    Marker corners are L-shapes:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b7bacbf/5/code.py:26:#   combo: the same tracing logic finds an irregular L-shaped cavity whose ring\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d8e07eb2/30/code.py:26:#      an L-shape with blue accents near the top; the later one is a zigzag with\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/d8e07eb2/30/code.py:30:#      and therefore highlights the earlier yellow-dominant L-shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/71e489b6/38/code.py:34:#    orthogonally convex blue regions (rectangles, separated rectangles, L-shapes)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/23/code.py:17:#    L pentomino whose missing corner indicates facing. We use one fixed family:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/23/code.py:77:#    be ambiguous. Because the missing corner rotates with motion, 90-degree turns\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/23/code.py:415:    Advance an L-shaped sprite through a walled frame and return the final pose.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/29/code.py:28:#    - top/bottom palettes are T-shaped and left/right palettes are L-shaped;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D9/0/code.py:47:#    - The generator builds an outer L-shaped structural barrier that touches the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D19/1/code.py:24:#    - new input: a 3-pixel L-shaped magenta marker at the same corner -> new\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/23/code.py:298:    - Black background with two dominant foreground colors occupying large rectangular/L-shaped regions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/34/code.py:110:    raise AssertionError(\"missing corner alignment legend\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/de809cff/6/code.py:51:#    against clipped wedges/L-shapes in the same color system.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/25/code.py:12:#    - Small example: if the missing corner is top-left, the top endpoint points left and the left endpoint\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/25/code.py:19:#    - The wall is restricted to a 1-pixel rectangular frame with exactly one missing corner. This keeps the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/25/code.py:364:    - The background is the most common color. The most frequent non-background color is a wall that forms a thin enclosure with one missing corner, so its opening points diagonally.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/25/code.py:371:    Key insight: The wall endpoints no longer indicate a single up/down/left/right exit; instead they sit on adjacent sides of a missing corner, and their outward vectors combine into the diagonal that governs both the fill wedge and the mover displacement.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D1/0/code.py:38:#      collapse to a thin L-shape and make the task visually trivial.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/78332cb0/D9/2/code.py:50:      an L-shape or left a cavity.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/5/code.py:41:#      thin L-shape. The generator therefore uses the same one-bend fan-out as\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f3a5a89/12/code.py:244:    # Base L-shaped barrier that makes the marker-reachable room exactly the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/35ab12c3/3/code.py:12:#      geometry is the L-shaped 4-cell walk that first travels 2 cells along the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/35ab12c3/3/code.py:63:#        * geometry is unmistakably L-shaped knight motion instead of straight rays\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/35ab12c3/3/code.py:325:L-shaped walk with a dashed rhythm tied to the number of visible vertices.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/17/code.py:17:#       near blocker: an L-shape whose right wall is closer to the separator\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/17/code.py:33:#   - The object vocabulary stays small: closed shell emitters, one L-shaped blocker, and at most no\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/17/code.py:278:    \"\"\"L-shape with a full right wall and a top bar placed outside the emitter's overlap rows.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/446ef5d2/11/code.py:31:#       3-cell L-shaped color triplets so the removed marker does not visually reappear.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/10/code.py:303:    \"\"\"Build a non-emitter distractor sprite (C-shape, L-shape, or solid block).\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/446ef5d2/15/code.py:19:#      whole-rectangle reflection, then draw a 1-pixel-wide monochrome L-shaped trail from the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/446ef5d2/15/code.py:58:# - Trail paths are center-to-center L-shapes, so every trail stays in-bounds automatically once\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/446ef5d2/15/code.py:437:    marker-colored L-shaped trails from each source piece to its reflected target box.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/13/code.py:209:    - In that slid state, inspect each component's bbox and treat any background recess that reaches the inner face next to the separator as a trigger, even if the recess is open like a C-shape or L-shape, provided it is backed by a black right wall and also touches some other black edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D3/2/code.py:173:    - Continue the marker to the boundary one tile-unit at a time, alternating original orientation and a mirror along the ray axis.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D3/2/code.py:309:    \"\"\"Build a small asymmetric seed whose mirror along the ray axis is visibly different.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/22/code.py:46:#   L-shaped path whose vertical leg length equals the hole height.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/22/code.py:78:#   and the red signal is no longer a set of full-width rows but an L-shaped trace hugging the divider.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/22/code.py:87:#   stays legible even when multiple emitters contribute nearby L-shapes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/35ab12c3/30/code.py:21:#      Fused output draws only the L-shape (top + right), and the shadow keeps\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cbebaa4b/24/code.py:24:#    Example trace: in the original puzzle a scattered green piece might be an L-shape with two\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/446ef5d2/22/code.py:31:#   Old logic: search for an L-shaped color with count 3, derive a corner, then test many\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1818057f/8/code.py:78:#    - Extra noise is limited to small lines/L-shapes/blocks whose local degree\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cbebaa4b/D1/3/code.py:363:    \"\"\"Draw an L-shaped path from *start* to *end*, preserving connector pixels.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cbebaa4b/D12/0/code.py:330:    \"\"\"Draw an L-shaped path from *start* to *end*, preserving red (2) pixels.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d59b0160/D3/2/code.py:18:#     - Old task: solver scanned the top-left corner for an L-shaped border, then read target colors from one compact 3x3 interior.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/8/code.py:402:    - An optional 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker is also fully embedded inside one stripe.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/8/code.py:409:    - A 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker controls rotation: top-right corner means rotate 90 degrees counterclockwise, and top-left corner means rotate 90 degrees clockwise.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cbebaa4b/D13/1/code.py:413:    \"\"\"Draw an L-shaped path from *start* to *end*, preserving red (2) pixels.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/1/code.py:410:    - An optional 5-cell L-shaped marker of color 9 sits inside one region and encodes a 90-degree rotation of the final output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1818057f/4/code.py:50:#   missing corner\" does not. Because many samples repeat this contrast, the rule is inferable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/9/code.py:169:    Extend diagonal rays from L-shaped corner markers around hollow square rings on a checkerboard.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cbebaa4b/D6/0/code.py:317:    \"\"\"Draw an L-shaped path from *start* to *end*, preserving red (2) pixels.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b3084d4/19/code.py:11:#    - an L-shape with a missing bottom-right corner, or\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b3084d4/19/code.py:278:    - Return the tight bounding box of that assembly, leaving the missing corner/notch as 0.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/21/code.py:52:#     short outer glyphs are L-shaped instead of straight, and only the upward-facing Ls elongate.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/3/code.py:390:    Repaint regions from L-shaped control markers, erase those markers, and optionally rotate the result using a color-9 L marker.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/11/code.py:29:#   single L-shaped leftover region. A sprite lying above or below the template is mirrored\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/11/code.py:356:    \"\"\"Find a 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker and return its corner position.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1818057f/14/code.py:146:    Key insight: The solver must recognize a broken rotationally symmetric cross from its asymmetric L-shaped fragment. Detection is done on the original input only, and each detected elbow is expanded to the unique full '+' centered at the same pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/12/code.py:32:       an L-shaped red marker. Its corner is the anchor, and the payload reflects\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/12/code.py:481:    - L-shaped red marker -> diagonal reflection\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/cbebaa4b/D11/2/code.py:28:#      L-shaped arrangement. It still contains red, but every attempted red-on-red translation\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/10/code.py:15:#       - Input: a blue (1) L-shape sits below a red horizontal line.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/15/code.py:428:    Recolor boundary-marked regions by averaging palette positions, then optionally rotate with an L-shaped 9 marker.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/35ab12c3/D2/0/code.py:38:#    - Corner-triplet groups visibly become L-shapes instead of closed triangles,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/20/code.py:71:# - The optional L-shaped color-9 marker is placed only inside one fragment and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/20/code.py:338:    \"\"\"Find a 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker and return its corner position.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/35ab12c3/D2/2/code.py:11:#    is (2,1) or (1,2). The filled path is the unique canonical \"2 then 1\" L-shape,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/35ab12c3/D2/2/code.py:42:#    repeated L-shaped bends. Because the input still only shows sparse vertices, the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/8/code.py:67:     1. the mover is visibly L-shaped rather than square;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/8/code.py:69:     3. the red goal is a larger docking frame with an L-shaped blue notch, and reachable outputs keep that frame\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/2/code.py:9:#      scraps, and an optional 5-cell L-shaped color-9 rotation marker.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/2/code.py:346:    \"\"\"Find a 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker and return its corner position.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/33/code.py:28:     3. The destination is a red docking frame whose inner cavity is an L-shaped blue notch\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/16/code.py:359:    \"\"\"Find a 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker and return its corner position.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/11/code.py:76:#    the output reads as a large L-shape plus a blocking vertical lane instead of a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/10/code.py:319:    \"\"\"Find a 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker and return its corner position.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b80bb43/16/code.py:12:#       That 2x2 box is centered off the gap midpoint by one step, so the missing corner is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/7/code.py:59:#      become longer L-shaped paths; parity would create fake nodes on the arms. The fused solver\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b80bb43/5/code.py:24:#   \"longer diagonal chain\" remains visible inside the new L-shaped family.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/4/code.py:526:    \"\"\"Find a 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker and return its corner position.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D15/1/code.py:80:#   - main() assumes marker components are color-5 L-shapes of area 3. The\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/13/code.py:266:    - An optional 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker may be embedded inside one region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/19/code.py:42:#      repeated L-shaped local marks. That prevents the fusion from collapsing\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/23/code.py:338:    - There is no L-shaped rotation marker in this variant.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/6/code.py:63:#      to confuse with the original \"overlap becomes O\" behavior once a few missing corner cells appear.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/6/code.py:365:    \"\"\"Find a 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker and return its corner position.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e87109e9/36/code.py:20:      - the visible delta is therefore not just a different legend glyph: the output shows both a bounce-back corridor and a missing corner after quota exhaustion\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/14/code.py:310:    - There is no separate L-shaped rotation sprite.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/f560132c/D5/2/code.py:36:     legend piece, generation keeps a geometrically distinctive L-shaped anchor piece and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/f560132c/D5/2/code.py:411:LEGEND_THRESHOLD = {8: 4, 10: 5, 12: 9}        # min extent threshold per side for anchor L-shape\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/f560132c/D5/2/code.py:413:LEGEND_ARM_RANGE = range(1, 4)                 # arm width/height options for L-shape construction\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/f560132c/D5/2/code.py:464:    \"\"\"Build an L-shaped anchor piece mask anchored at (0,0) of the side*side grid.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/18/code.py:334:    \"\"\"Place an L-shaped divider with the legend panel in one corner.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/18/code.py:80:# --- L-shape templates ---\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/18/code.py:185:    \"\"\"Return info about the missing corner rectangle inside an L-shape bbox.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/18/code.py:214:    \"\"\"Build a valid L-shape spec, or None if the geometry fails the fusion constraints.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/18/code.py:247:    \"\"\"Enumerate all legal L-shape specs in random order.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/18/code.py:341:    Build a red cascade by activating L-shaped blue blobs whose short arm end is a hidden port.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/18/code.py:344:    - bg = most common color. Blue objects are asymmetric filled L-shapes with no green markers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/18/code.py:348:    - Shoot a thin ray upward from the start; when it first hits a blue L-shape, recolor that whole blob red.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/18/code.py:352:    Key insight: The firing side is encoded by geometry alone: the short arm tip of each L-shape is the only extreme edge with length 1-2, so its direction and ray thickness can be inferred from the silhouette.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/18/code.py:401:    # --- STEP 3) Extract blue blobs and infer each hidden port from its L-shaped silhouette ---\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/18/code.py:469:    # --- STEP 5) BFS propagate: every activated L-shape emits from its hidden port ---\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/18/code.py:610:    \"\"\"Place one off-path distractor L-shape if space exists.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/35ab12c3/D6/1/code.py:19:#   old output: draw the L-shape in 2, draw the shifted copy in 7 only on bg cells,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/f560132c/D2/3/code.py:356:LEGEND_THRESHOLD = {8: 4, 10: 5, 12: 9}       # min extent threshold per side for legend L-shape\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/f560132c/D2/3/code.py:358:LEGEND_ARM_RANGE = range(1, 4)                 # arm width/height options for L-shape construction\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/f560132c/D2/3/code.py:404:    \"\"\"Build an L-shaped legend piece mask anchored at (0,0) of the side*side grid.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/19/code.py:362:    \"\"\"Place an L-shaped divider with legend panel in one corner.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/27/code.py:370:    \"\"\"Place an L-shaped divider with the legend panel in one corner.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/4/code.py:46:#    - Divider layouts remain full-row, full-column, or L-shaped, so the legend\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/4/code.py:387:    \"\"\"Place an L-shaped divider with the legend panel tucked into one corner.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/24/code.py:383:    \"\"\"Place an L-shaped divider with a corner panel.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/5/code.py:339:    \"\"\"Place an L-shaped divider with legend panel in one corner.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/33/code.py:38:    plus one detached L-shaped noise blob elsewhere\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/33/code.py:44:    1. Reject 