mines the global post-assembly rotation direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/f560132c/D15/0/code.py:421:    \"\"\"Build an L-shaped legend piece whose longer arm encodes the final rotation direction.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/30/code.py:367:    \"\"\"Place an L-shaped divider with a legend panel in one corner.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/32/code.py:375:    \"\"\"Place an L-shaped divider with the legend panel in one corner.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/17/code.py:400:    \"\"\"Place an L-shaped divider with legend panel in one corner.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/12/code.py:353:    \"\"\"Place an L-shaped divider with legend panel in one corner.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/2/code.py:41:  2x5(area 10) -> 3x4(area 12), while the L-shape disappears completely.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a251c730/36/code.py:21:#    L-shaped trail between the two rectangles. The wallpaper itself changes from axial stripes to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/2/code.py:25:#    - Small example: suppose a pink legend is an L-shaped ring with 2 holes. A grey\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/2/code.py:26:#      L-shaped sprite with 1 hole still matches because both fill to the same solid\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b0039139/8/code.py:34:#    D2-only would output the L-shape from the zero-mask crop. This combo instead fills\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b0039139/8/code.py:35:#    the missing corner and outputs a 2x2 block. The original base solver would be more\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b0039139/8/code.py:70:#    convex than that cut-out, often filling an obvious missing corner. Because the stencil\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/9/code.py:411:    \"\"\"Place an L-shaped divider with legend panel in one corner.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/10/code.py:380:    \"\"\"Place an L-shaped divider with a legend line tucked into one corner.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/21/code.py:460:    \"\"\"Place an L-shaped divider with legend panel in one corner.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/29/code.py:72:#    output contains whole rows or whole columns rather than corner L-shapes, so\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/8/code.py:268:    Route each solid sender's missing corner-set to a shared receiver hub, completing stacked solids.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a47bf94d/8/code.py:278:    - The missing corner-set travels along the attached wire to the far endpoint's nominal anchor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/25/code.py:331:    - Exactly one outer starter component touches the ring in two places and behaves like the original L-shaped source.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/bf45cf4b/18/code.py:67:- The group layout is limited to row / column / L-shape arrangements, which stays readable and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/18/code.py:18:#      A: sparse L-shape -> rotated sparse L-shape\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/25/code.py:31:#      test src: an L-shaped path\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/35/code.py:45:#    - The generator keeps the closed frame, 1px border, and external L-shapes from the base task.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D1/0/code.py:50:#     - Motifs are asymmetric because each logical 2x3 pattern has one missing corner,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/16/code.py:8:#   an L-shaped open rectangle. The solver reads which top/bottom side and which\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:68:#      1. blue L-shapes identify arrow tips and directions;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:379:    - The background is the most common color. Active blue objects are 3-cell L-shaped arrows; the degree-2 corner is the tip and the missing diagonal quadrant gives the arrow's facing direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/10/code.py:34:# - Candidate paths are restricted to a small family of corner-based L-shapes, with\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/4/code.py:17:#    - I restrict ring-touching components to L-shapes. Each sample uses one shared 3-color cycle\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/4/code.py:258:    - Outside the frame are simple L-shaped open rectangles whose two path endpoints touch the ring\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/28/code.py:12:#      L-shapes or a 3-cell T-like motif. That cue is NOT rotated; it encodes the payload's\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:268:    - bg = most common color. Blue source objects are 3-cell L-shaped arrows whose corner cell is the tip and whose missing quadrant gives the forward diagonal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/6/code.py:277:    - Neither raw blue geometry nor marker colors alone are sufficient: the L-shape identifies the true tip and diagonal direction, while the repeated marker color decides which two arrows should actually be connected.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3a25b0d8/29/code.py:52:#       s3 blue L-shape empty\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/34/code.py:248:    \"\"\"Build a straight or L-shaped Manhattan path between two points.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/36/code.py:12:#      source is an ordinary L-shaped open rectangle whose far outer elbow carries one extra cell,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a6f40cea/36/code.py:585:    - Genuine traces are thin 1-cell-wide L-shaped open frames; fake traces look similar but include\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/14/code.py:23:#     train src (5x5): a red 3-cell line in one corner and a blue L-shape in the opposite corner.\n